(73808, 2450, 1005, '<td valign="top">Kinda creepy effect (I hope you were going for that!)  I will bet you are getting shadow distintion comments, same as me.  Try moving your light source farther away, it tends to sharpen the shadow edges.  (I ran out of extension cord)   I would also suggest cropping out the plants in the foreground and if possible, a less harsh light, see how the middle of the light washes out everything? Also a bit grainy.<br/>Photo 7 Creativity 6 Shadows 7 total 7</td>', 'Kinda creepy effect (I hope you were going for that!)  I will bet you are getting shadow distintion comments, same as me.  Try moving your light source farther away, it tends to sharpen the shadow edges.  (I ran out of extension cord)   I would also suggest cropping out the plants in the foreground and if possible, a less harsh light, see how the middle of the light washes out everything? Also a bit grainy.Photo 7 Creativity 6 Shadows 7 total 7', '2002-06-17 19:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
