(73990, 2457, 772, '<td valign="top">This is more of a ''ghost'' than a shadow but I like the way this photograph was executed... There is a little grain in the photo that may not be necessary but, overall, this photo works for me :)  I would almost rather see this shot in a vertical crop completely removing the white portion of the wall in this photo.  Good work!</td>', 'This is more of a ''ghost'' than a shadow but I like the way this photograph was executed... There is a little grain in the photo that may not be necessary but, overall, this photo works for me :)  I would almost rather see this shot in a vertical crop completely removing the white portion of the wall in this photo.  Good work!', '2002-06-18 19:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(73991, 2457, 1037, '<td valign="top">This is a lovely image. What seemed to be a reflection actually appears to be a double exposure. I understand how this can be an interpretation of a shadow... in a ghostly sense. I think the low contrast works with that (I''m sure some people will say this is grey and grey rather than black and white)</td>', 'This is a lovely image. What seemed to be a reflection actually appears to be a double exposure. I understand how this can be an interpretation of a shadow... in a ghostly sense. I think the low contrast works with that (I''m sure some people will say this is grey and grey rather than black and white)', '2002-06-19 04:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(73992, 2457, 2188, '<td valign="top">Fun interpretation of the challenge.</td>', 'Fun interpretation of the challenge.', '2002-06-19 10:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(73993, 2457, 1005, '<td valign="top">I hope you were going for an interpretation of the challenge, I think.  I can appreciate that, but this is still pushing my flexability a bit too far.   The double image could be said to be "a shadow of herself", but the challenge intent was around lighting, not philosophy.  See the back of the ladies arm?  That''s shadow and that''s what I am going to score you against.  Photo 5 Creativity 7 (it''s creative, but outside the challenge) Shadows 2 Total 4</td>', 'I hope you were going for an interpretation of the challenge, I think.  I can appreciate that, but this is still pushing my flexability a bit too far.   The double image could be said to be "a shadow of herself", but the challenge intent was around lighting, not philosophy.  See the back of the ladies arm?  That''s shadow and that''s what I am going to score you against.  Photo 5 Creativity 7 (it''s creative, but outside the challenge) Shadows 2 Total 4', '2002-06-19 18:07:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(73994, 2457, 737, '<td valign="top">Interesting intrepretation. Good job.</td>', 'Interesting intrepretation. Good job.', '2002-06-20 12:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
