(74516, 2503, 244, '<td valign="top">I love the lighting and the angle of this shot, it gives a really nice feel.  The "blown out" area in the window helps to add to the darkness of the shadow areas.  Nice Job.    Score 8 ------- Corey</td>', 'I love the lighting and the angle of this shot, it gives a really nice feel.  The "blown out" area in the window helps to add to the darkness of the shadow areas.  Nice Job.    Score 8 ------- Corey', '2002-06-22 01:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(74517, 2503, 2111, '<td valign="top">Fantastic job! So unplanned looking. (7)</td>', 'Fantastic job! So unplanned looking. (7)', '2002-06-22 11:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(74518, 2503, 1061, '<td valign="top">Great photo</td>', 'Great photo', '2002-06-23 04:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(74519, 2503, 1547, '<td valign="top">Photographers comments:  The picture was taken in the dining room of a small English style Bed &amp; Breakfast Inn outside of San Francisco.  I did not rearrange anything before taking the picture; this is exactly how I found the setting. <br/><br/>That''s a dining table on the lower right.  Because of the slow shutter speed I set my camera on the table and used it as a tripod.  I received several comments asking about  the chairs on the left - they look out of place (too high) because they were on top of a bench in order to get them out of the way during the daytime when they weren''t needed for dining.<br/><br/>My thanks to everyone for their voting and comments.  This was my first submission to DP Challenge and I found it challenging, enlightening and a lot of fun.<br/><br/></td>', 'Photographers comments:  The picture was taken in the dining room of a small English style Bed & Breakfast Inn outside of San Francisco.  I did not rearrange anything before taking the picture; this is exactly how I found the setting. That''s a dining table on the lower right.  Because of the slow shutter speed I set my camera on the table and used it as a tripod.  I received several comments asking about  the chairs on the left - they look out of place (too high) because they were on top of a bench in order to get them out of the way during the daytime when they weren''t needed for dining.My thanks to everyone for their voting and comments.  This was my first submission to DP Challenge and I found it challenging, enlightening and a lot of fun.', '2002-06-24 01:51:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(74520, 2505, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very nice.  I like how the color gradiates up the frame, but to pick nit, I would have like the upper arm to continue this vein.  You are going to get grain comments, don''t let them bother you.  In this case, you get a bespeckled look that others would have to achieve in Photoshop.  The grain is very consistant and reminds me of the painting style (can''t remember the name) that was popular at the turn of the century, using paint dots, you know.<br/>Photo 8 Creativity 7 Shadows 9 total 8</td>', 'Very nice.  I like how the color gradiates up the frame, but to pick nit, I would have like the upper arm to continue this vein.  You are going to get grain comments, don''t let them bother you.  In this case, you get a bespeckled look that others would have to achieve in Photoshop.  The grain is very consistant and reminds me of the painting style (can''t remember the name) that was popular at the turn of the century, using paint dots, you know.Photo 8 Creativity 7 Shadows 9 total 8', '2002-06-17 13:51:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(74521, 2505, 616, '<td valign="top">Nice curves, but the photo seems a bit grainy.</td>', 'Nice curves, but the photo seems a bit grainy.', '2002-06-17 14:24:00.000000', NULL, 1),
