(75482, 2573, 313, '<td valign="top">d0od, i don''t get it.  like, there''s a shadow but wtf?  <br/><br/>just kidding.  i really like the blue, and the shadows falling on the stone are very interestingly shaped.</td>', 'd0od, i don''t get it.  like, there''s a shadow but wtf?  just kidding.  i really like the blue, and the shadows falling on the stone are very interestingly shaped.', '2002-06-23 23:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(75483, 2573, 1454, '<td valign="top">Interesting topic... I liked it.</td>', 'Interesting topic... I liked it.', '2002-06-23 23:32:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(75484, 2573, 312, '<td valign="top">For the record, the title for this shot has nothing to do with the photograph itself. It has more to do with my state of mind when I went out to shoot. And if you don''t think the "shadows" are the focus of the shot, then you''re not looking at it right. Tilt your head to the left and then bang it against a wall. Now you should be seeing it like I do.<br/><br/>I broke a personal rule with this photo, and that''s never to take a pretentious shot of a tombstone and try to pass it off as art. However, I saw it as less of a shot of a tombstone and more of a shot of the shadows on the stone. If it had been a white wall with those shadows I would have been just as happy with the shot.<br/><br/>Setzler - I chose to duotone this shot because the color one sucked. All the green trees in the background really took over and didn''t let the contrasts show through. I also thought the use of just light and "shadow" would accentuate the shadow more than the surroundings, but I guess I was wrong.</td>', 'For the record, the title for this shot has nothing to do with the photograph itself. It has more to do with my state of mind when I went out to shoot. And if you don''t think the "shadows" are the focus of the shot, then you''re not looking at it right. Tilt your head to the left and then bang it against a wall. Now you should be seeing it like I do.I broke a personal rule with this photo, and that''s never to take a pretentious shot of a tombstone and try to pass it off as art. However, I saw it as less of a shot of a tombstone and more of a shot of the shadows on the stone. If it had been a white wall with those shadows I would have been just as happy with the shot.Setzler - I chose to duotone this shot because the color one sucked. All the green trees in the background really took over and didn''t let the contrasts show through. I also thought the use of just light and "shadow" would accentuate the shadow more than the surroundings, but I guess I was wrong.', '2002-06-24 01:47:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(75485, 2574, 1054, '<td valign="top">Nice composition, great interpretation of the theme.</td>', 'Nice composition, great interpretation of the theme.', '2002-06-17 17:55:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(75486, 2574, 1005, '<td valign="top">Nice, simple, do I see your reflection in the mask?  Photo 8 Creativity 7 Shadows 8 total 8</td>', 'Nice, simple, do I see your reflection in the mask?  Photo 8 Creativity 7 Shadows 8 total 8', '2002-06-18 14:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(75487, 2574, 1037, '<td valign="top">The irridescent colours of the mask are very beautiful. There isn''t much emphasis on the shadow, but it''s there, and the themes of masks and identity are interesting.</td>', 'The irridescent colours of the mask are very beautiful. There isn''t much emphasis on the shadow, but it''s there, and the themes of masks and identity are interesting.', '2002-06-19 07:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(75488, 2574, 693, '<td valign="top">There is a reflection in the mask which is barely visible yet distracting enough.  Also the highlights being reflected off of the mask are blinding and could use some softening.</td>', 'There is a reflection in the mask which is barely visible yet distracting enough.  Also the highlights being reflected off of the mask are blinding and could use some softening.', '2002-06-19 12:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(75489, 2574, 1, '<td valign="top">I like the idea, but something went wrong w/ the presentation.  The mask is too reflective, and the flash/lighting used reflects too much off it.</td>', 'I like the idea, but something went wrong w/ the presentation.  The mask is too reflective, and the flash/lighting used reflects too much off it.', '2002-06-19 15:51:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(75490, 2574, 772, '<td valign="top">very nice!  I have no critique for improvement on this shot at all... i suppose that whatever is reflecting in the mask above the nose seems a bit strange but I do like this photo! = 9 - jmsetzler</td>', 'very nice!  I have no critique for improvement on this shot at all... i suppose that whatever is reflecting in the mask above the nose seems a bit strange but I do like this photo! = 9 - jmsetzler', '2002-06-20 18:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(75491, 2574, 1041, '<td valign="top">Cool idea.  What''s the material of the mask?  It seems very reflective, you have some hotspots on it.  You may be able to reduce those by putting tissue paper over your lightsource.  I''d suggest not pointing the lightsource directly at the mask, but then you wouldn''t get the shadow, would you! ;)  If there is any way of not having the shadow from your hand holding the mask showing that would be a bonus.  Not sure if that''s doable though, so please ignore the comment if it wasn''t.</td>', 'Cool idea.  What''s the material of the mask?  It seems very reflective, you have some hotspots on it.  You may be able to reduce those by putting tissue paper over your lightsource.  I''d suggest not pointing the lightsource directly at the mask, but then you wouldn''t get the shadow, would you! ;)  If there is any way of not having the shadow from your hand holding the mask showing that would be a bonus.  Not sure if that''s doable though, so please ignore the comment if it wasn''t.', '2002-06-21 18:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(75492, 2574, 637, '<td valign="top">Would like the shadow to be sharper.</td>', 'Would like the shadow to be sharper.', '2002-06-23 02:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(75493, 2576, 1897, '<td valign="top">three is a magic number</td>', 'three is a magic number', '2002-06-17 13:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(75494, 2576, 436, '<td valign="top">spiffy concept well-executed</td>', 'spiffy concept well-executed', '2002-06-17 14:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(75495, 2576, 1175, '<td valign="top">Very cool.</td>', 'Very cool.', '2002-06-17 14:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(75496, 2576, 570, '<td valign="top">kinda dumb</td>', 'kinda dumb', '2002-06-17 14:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(75497, 2576, 1005, '<td valign="top">Some interesting shadows.....shot taken in a corner, maybe?  left side wall vs. right side wall soooo different, was that on purpose?  Do you have zoom capabilities?  If so, try this, move as far back as you can and still zoom to this framing, I think you would get an overall better focus on more of your subjects.  You might also get a better flash fill, too.  Right middle of frame is white overblown, sign of too much flash.<br/>Photo 6 Creativity 7 Shadows 7 total 7</td>', 'Some interesting shadows.....shot taken in a corner, maybe?  left side wall vs. right side wall soooo different, was that on purpose?  Do you have zoom capabilities?  If so, try this, move as far back as you can and still zoom to this framing, I think you would get an overall better focus on more of your subjects.  You might also get a better flash fill, too.  Right middle of frame is white overblown, sign of too much flash.Photo 6 Creativity 7 Shadows 7 total 7', '2002-06-17 18:07:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(75498, 2576, 1054, '<td valign="top">I don''t mind setup shots, but this is a bit *too* contrived for my taste.</td>', 'I don''t mind setup shots, but this is a bit *too* contrived for my taste.', '2002-06-17 18:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
